[["page","lines",0],{"text":"time point or in AUC were observed between REx and SED conditions. There were also no","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":105.05509477807993,"width":430.2918442568421,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",1],{"text":"differences in ratings of appeal or desire to eat high- or low-calorie food images,","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":123.53508738608002,"width":377.986517207566,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",2],{"text":"Supplementary Table 2.","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":141.77508009008,"width":120.2256701294863,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",3],{"text":"3.3 Ad libitum dietary intake","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":166.13507034607994,"width":131.61118513487125,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",4],{"text":"As shown in Table 2, there were no differences in ad libitum energy intake between conditions.","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":184.61506295408003,"width":449.3858251633005,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",5],{"text":"Similarly, there were also no differences in macronutrient composition of the meal between REx","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":203.21505551408006,"width":452.3709154106157,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",6],{"text":"and SED conditions.","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":221.69504812208004,"width":97.18582889996173,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",7],{"text":"Table 2. Ab libitum dietary intake during a single meal after resistance exercise (REx) or","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":270.17502873007993,"width":446.3775225290316,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",8],{"text":"sedentary conditions (SED)","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":282.41502383408,"width":139.8966777395954,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",9],{"text":"Ad libitum parameter REx (n=16) SED (n=15) p","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":75.59996976,"y":296.21501831408,"width":361.0414371178806,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",10],{"text":"Energy intake, kcal 722 \u00b1 100 663 \u00b1 92 0.496","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":75.59996976,"y":310.13501274607995,"width":381.3325220053446,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",11],{"text":"Energy intake, kcal/kg body mass 10.8 \u00b1 1.5 9.8 \u00b1 1.4 0.304","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":75.59996976,"y":322.97500761008007,"width":381.3316399377878,"height":10.745195701919954}]
[["page","lines",12],{"text":"Carbohydrates, % energy intake 49.9 \u00b1 1.9 48.3 \u00b1 1.9 0.371","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":75.59996976,"y":335.69500252208,"width":381.331455730931,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",13],{"text":"Fat, % energy intake 36.3 \u00b1 2.1 39.5 \u00b1 2.1 0.170","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":75.59996976,"y":348.53499738607997,"width":381.33255368563573,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",14],{"text":"Protein, % energy intake 16.1 \u00b1 0.7 14.6 \u00b1 1.0 0.120","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":75.59996976,"y":361.25499229807997,"width":381.33107766705507,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",15],{"text":"Presented as mean \u00b1 standard error. Meals were provided 180 minutes following the completion","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":375.05498677808,"width":455.3716572887661,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",16],{"text":"of a standardized breakfast meal and 90 minutes after completion of either REx or SED","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":387.41498183408004,"width":413.1148236929732,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",17],{"text":"conditions.","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":399.65497693808,"width":51.22564247609296,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",18],{"text":"3.4 Ghrelin and peptide-YY","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":424.37496705008,"width":129.20342830684734,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",19],{"text":"There were no differences in fasted or AUC values of ghrelin or PYY between conditions,","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":442.85495965808,"width":421.4265487894729,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",20],{"text":"Figure 4. However, ghrelin was lower during the REx condition 120 (765 \u00b1 70 vs. 859 \u00b1 94","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":461.09495236208,"width":428.49116399078184,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",21],{"text":"pg/mL, p=0.031) and 180 (941 \u00b1 81 vs. 1046 \u00b1 105 pg/mL, p=0.018) minutes post-breakfast,","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":479.57494497007997,"width":436.78606909490145,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",22],{"text":"with trends observed 90 (754 \u00b1 64 vs. 828 \u00b1 84 pg/mL, p=0.094) and 150 (838 \u00b1 71 vs. 921 \u00b1 94","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":498.17493753008,"width":455.4914519871868,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",23],{"text":"pg/mL, p=0.086) minutes after breakfast. Compared to SED, PYY was higher during the REx","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":516.77493009008,"width":439.05072872662925,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",24],{"text":"condition 90 (159 \u00b1 9 vs. 135 \u00b1 10 pg/mL, p=0.028) and 120 (157 \u00b1 8 vs. 138 \u00b1 8 pg/mL,","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":535.25492269808,"width":417.3463269747085,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",25],{"text":"p=0.041) minutes post-breakfast. Ghrelin AUC and PYY AUC were not correlated to any dietary","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":553.61491535408,"width":452.7304005409791,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",26],{"text":"intake or VAS AUC parameter in either condition (data not presented).","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":572.09490796208,"width":332.1454503104631,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",27],{"text":"3.5 Correlations","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":609.05489317808,"width":75.68980085166498,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",28],{"text":"Ad libitum energy intake adjusted for body mass was positively correlated to PFC AUC","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":627.41488583408,"width":409.5145507156823,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",29],{"text":"(r=0.556, p=0.031) during the SED condition only; no other correlations between energy intake","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":645.89487844208,"width":447.0913210749537,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",30],{"text":"and VAS AUC or food images were observed in either condition. Correlations among VAS AUC","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":664.37487105008,"width":451.27488861408415,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",31],{"text":"parameters and energy intake with body composition and RMR are shown in Table 3. In the","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":682.8548636580799,"width":435.2117968234896,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",32],{"text":"REx condition, satiety AUC was positively correlated with FFM, with no other significant","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":701.45485621808,"width":413.0261820769565,"height":10.74519570192001}]
[["page","lines",33],{"text":"correlations observed. In the SED condition, hunger AUC and PFC AUC were negatively","fontSize":10.74519570192,"x":70.079971968,"y":719.81484887408,"width":419.1305117291682,"height":10.74519570192001}]
